Falsifies `paging::domain::a_grant_the_domain_cannot_express_is_refused`.

The defect: a region whose `base + size` wraps `u64` is accepted. The check is the newer of the
two guards and the one whose absence is hardest to notice, because a wrapping region is not a
region: it has no end, so "inside the grant" is not a statement that can be made about it, and
the code that would notice is the code that computes the limit. `grant_pages`'s doc is careful
that this is a proof obligation closed rather than a reachable bug fixed, and that is exactly
why it needs a proof: no caller can construct such a region today, so nothing but this harness
stands between the check and somebody deleting it as dead weight.

Expected to fail: `assert!(grant_pages(r).is_err(), "a grant no page-granular domain can express
exactly was accepted")`, for any page-aligned `base` with a `size` large enough to wrap, the
smallest being `base = 2^64 - 4096` with `size = 4096`.

The alignment guard above it is broken by the `an_enumerated_page_lies_inside_the_grant` record
instead.

diff --git a/crates/paging/src/domain.rs b/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
--- a/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
+++ b/crates/paging/src/domain.rs
@@ -71,9 +71,6 @@ pub fn grant_pages(r: DmaRegion) -> Result<u64, MapError> {
     if !r.base.is_multiple_of(PAGE_SIZE) {
         return Err(MapError::Misaligned);
     }
-    if r.base.checked_add(r.size).is_none() {
-        return Err(MapError::BadRegion);
-    }
     Ok(r.size / PAGE_SIZE)
 }
 
